{"name":"Lady-In-Waiting","hex":"#aedcec","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"lady-in-waiting","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A lady, often a noblewoman, in the household of a queen, princess, or other woman of higher rank who attends her as a personal assistant, generally a role considered an honour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lady-in-waiting"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lady-in-waiting","blocks":[{"text":"A lady-in-waiting or court lady is a female personal assistant at a court, attending on a royal woman or a high-ranking noblewoman. Historically, in Europe, a lady-in-waiting was often a noblewoman but of lower rank than the woman to whom she attended. Although she may or may not have received financial or other compensation for her service, a lady-in-waiting was considered more of a secretary, courtier, or companion to her mistress than a servant."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Princess_Tatiana_Alexandrovna_Yusupova%2C_1858.jpg/330px-Princess_Tatiana_Alexandrovna_Yusupova%2C_1858.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lady-in-waiting","wikidata":"Q715222"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/A_palace_concert.jpg/500px-A_palace_concert.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/A_palace_concert.jpg/1280px-A_palace_concert.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/A_palace_concert.jpg/500px-A_palace_concert.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Tang dynasty court ladies on A Palace Concert painting","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AA_palace_concert.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Madame_la_princesse_de_Lamballe_by_Antoine-Fran%C3%A7ois_Callet_%28circa_1776%2C_Callet%29.jpg/500px-Madame_la_princesse_de_Lamballe_by_Antoine-Fran%C3%A7ois_Callet_%28circa_1776%2C_Callet%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Madame_la_princesse_de_Lamballe_by_Antoine-Fran%C3%A7ois_Callet_%28circa_1776%2C_Callet%29.jpg/1280px-Madame_la_princesse_de_Lamballe_by_Antoine-Fran%C3%A7ois_Callet_%28circa_1776%2C_Callet%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Madame_la_princesse_de_Lamballe_by_Antoine-Fran%C3%A7ois_Callet_%28circa_1776%2C_Callet%29.jpg/500px-Madame_la_princesse_de_Lamballe_by_Antoine-Fran%C3%A7ois_Callet_%28circa_1776%2C_Callet%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Marie Louise of Savoy-Carignan, Princesse de Lamballe was chief lady-in-waiting to Queen Marie Antoinette of France","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMadame_la_princesse_de_Lamballe_by_Antoine-Fran%C3%A7ois_Callet_(circa_1776%2C_Callet).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Wakefield_queen4.jpg/500px-Wakefield_queen4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Wakefield_queen4.jpg/500px-Wakefield_queen4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Countess of Airlie (right), a Lady of the Bedchamber, accompanying Queen Elizabeth II as her lady-in-waiting (March 2005).","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWakefield_queen4.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Royal_Visit_Toronto_2010_5.JPG/500px-Royal_Visit_Toronto_2010_5.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Royal_Visit_Toronto_2010_5.JPG/1280px-Royal_Visit_Toronto_2010_5.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Royal_Visit_Toronto_2010_5.JPG/500px-Royal_Visit_Toronto_2010_5.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Walking behind Queen Elizabeth II on a visit to Toronto in 2010 are two ladies-in-waiting: a Woman of the Bedchamber (Lady Susan Hussey, left, with white hat) and a Lady of the Bedchamber (Lady Farnham, right, with blue hat).","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARoyal_Visit_Toronto_2010_5.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Queen%27s_Companions_%26_Pages_%28SO%2724%29.jpg/500px-Queen%27s_Companions_%26_Pages_%28SO%2724%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Queen%27s_Companions_%26_Pages_%28SO%2724%29.jpg/500px-Queen%27s_Companions_%26_Pages_%28SO%2724%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Queen's companions the Marchioness of Lansdowne and Lady Sarah Keswick at the 2024 State Opening of Parliament","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AQueen's_Companions_%26_Pages_(SO'24).jpg"}],"sounds":{"lady-in-waiting":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/5e/En-us-lady-in-waiting.oga?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/5/5e/En-us-lady-in-waiting.oga/En-us-lady-in-waiting.oga.mp3"}]}}}